      "rationale": "Trailing whitespace in text does not change the output, except where 2 or more spaces make a hard line break. In code blocks it is part of the code.",
      "fix": "The fix deletes the trailing whitespace, or trims a hard line break to exactly 2 spaces. gomdlint reports some trailing whitespace without a fix, such as whitespace inside a code span, which is code, or a tab where the paragraph goes on to the next line, which some renderers read as a hard line break. gomdlint may report a finding without a fix when the fix would change a line with one character in brackets, such as [x] or [1], or the lines around it up to a blank line, because it could add or remove a task list checkbox. In a document with raw HTML other than comments and plain br, wbr, hr or img tags, gomdlint reports every finding without a fix.",
